{"name":"Bighorn Sheep","hex":"#20120e","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bighorn sheep","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Certain North American species of sheep","especially, Ovis canadensis, having large, curving horns."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bighorn_sheep"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bighorn sheep","blocks":[{"text":"The bighorn sheep or bighorn is a species of sheep native to North America. It is named for its large horns, a pair of them may weigh up to 14 kg (30 lb); the sheep altogether typically weigh up to 143 kg (315 lb). Recent genetic testing indicates three distinct subspecies of Ovis canadensis, one of which is endangered: O. c. sierrae."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/New_Mexico_Bighorn_Sheep.JPG/330px-New_Mexico_Bighorn_Sheep.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bighorn_sheep"},{"title":"Sheep","blocks":[{"text":"Sheep or domestic sheep are a domesticated ruminant mammal typically kept as livestock. Although the term sheep can apply to other species in the genus Ovis, in everyday usage it almost always refers to domesticated sheep. Like all ruminants, sheep are members of the order Artiodactyla, the even-toed ungulates. There are around 1.2 billion domestic sheep as of 2019, making them easily the most common species of sheep. An adult female is referred to as a ewe ; an intact male as a ram, occasionally a tup; a castrated male as a wether; and a young sheep as a lamb."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Flock_of_sheep.jpg/330px-Flock_of_sheep.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sheep"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg/500px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg/1280px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg/500px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABighorn_sheep_(Ovis_canadensis_canadensis)_female_Banff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg/500px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg/1280px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg/500px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_female_head_Banff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Female O. c. canadensisBanff National Park","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABighorn_sheep_(Ovis_canadensis_canadensis)_female_head_Banff.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_juvenile_Radium.jpg/500px-Bighorn_sheep_%28Ovis_canadensis_canadensis%29_juvenile_Radium.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser